---
import WysDecor from './WysDecor.astro';
import {Image} from 'astro:assets';
import WysPhoto from './WysPhoto.astro';
import {imageNotice} from '../data/wys.js';
const {example:e,number}=Astro.props;
const panels=['The whole package','Photographs','Pinterest','Instagram','Article','Products & copy'];
---
<section class:list={['wx-package',number===2&&'wx-package-lav']} id={e.slug} data-package>
 <div class="wx-folder-tab">WORKED EXAMPLE / 0{number}</div>
 <header class="wx-package-heading"><div><p class="wys-label">{e.category}</p><h2>{e.name}</h2><p>Follow one idea from the selected pieces to a complete content package.</p></div><a class="wys-text-link" href={`/lifestyle/${e.slug}`}>Read the live styling article →</a></header>
 <div class="wx-tabs" aria-label={`${e.name} package contents`}>{panels.map((p,i)=><button type="button" aria-pressed={i===0?'true':'false'} data-panel-button={i}>{p}</button>)}</div>
 <div data-panel="0" class="wx-panel"><div class="wx-output-label"><WysDecor class="wb-package-flower"/><h3>Open the files. See the whole idea.</h3><p>3 photographs · 3 Pins · 3 carousel slides · 1 article · 5 product records + copy</p></div>
  <div class="wx-contact">{e.photos.map((p,i)=><figure class={`wx-mini wb-photo-file mat-${i}`}><Image src={p.src} alt={p.alt} widths={[240,400]} sizes="(max-width:700px) 26vw, 280px"/><figcaption><b>PHOTO / 0{i+1}</b><span>{p.role}</span></figcaption></figure>)}{e.pins.map((p,i)=><figure class={`wx-mini wb-pin-file mat-${(i+1)%3}`}><Image src={p.src} alt={p.alt} widths={[240,400]} sizes="(max-width:700px) 26vw, 280px"/><figcaption><b>PINTEREST / 0{i+1}</b><span>{p.role} graphic</span></figcaption></figure>)}{e.slides.map((p,i)=><figure class={`wx-mini wb-slide-file mat-${(i+2)%3}`}><Image src={p.src} alt={p.alt} widths={[240,400]} sizes="(max-width:700px) 26vw, 280px"/><figcaption><b>INSTAGRAM / 0{i+1}</b><span>Carousel slide</span></figcaption></figure>)}</div>
  <div class="wx-paper-strip"><div><span class="wys-label">The written side, too</span><h3>{e.article.title}</h3><p>{e.article.intro}</p></div><div><b>Every piece has a job.</b><p>The product records, full article, Pin metadata and Instagram caption are in the tabs above. The same look stays connected across formats.</p></div></div>
 </div>
 <div data-panel="1" class="wx-panel"><div class="wx-output-label"><h3>Three views, three different jobs.</h3><p>The approved photographs, preserved at their original proportions.</p></div><div class="wx-three">{e.photos.map((p,i)=><WysPhoto photo={p} treatment={['double','lavender','polaroid'][i]} label={`${i+1} / ${p.role}`}/>)}</div><p class="wx-fine">{imageNotice}</p></div>
 <div data-panel="2" class="wx-panel"><div class="wx-output-label"><h3>A Pinterest set, with the copy.</h3><p>Three separate 1000 × 1500 graphics. Open the notes beneath each one.</p></div><div class="wx-three">{e.pins.map((p,i)=><div class={`wx-graphic mat-${i}`}><Image src={p.src} alt={p.alt} widths={[320,480,720,1000]} sizes="(max-width:700px) 80vw, 340px"/><div class="wx-graphic-copy"><span class="wys-label">Pin / 0{i+1} · {p.role}</span><details><summary>Read this Pin’s complete copy</summary><h4>Title</h4><p>{p.title}</p><h4>Description</h4><p>{p.description}</p><h4>Alt text</h4><p>{p.alt}</p><h4>Article destination</h4><a class="wys-text-link" href={p.destination}>{e.article.title} →</a><p class="wx-fine">Publication draft. Affiliate destinations remain pending.</p></details></div></div>)}</div></div>
 <div data-panel="3" class="wx-panel"><div class="wx-output-label"><h3>The swipe-through version.</h3><p>Three 1080 × 1350 slides: pieces → styled scene → lifestyle moment. Swipe on your phone or use the arrows.</p></div><div class="wx-slide-controls"><button type="button" data-slide-step="-1" aria-label={`Previous ${e.name} Instagram slide`}>← Previous</button><span aria-live="polite" data-slide-count>1 / 3</span><button type="button" data-slide-step="1" aria-label={`Next ${e.name} Instagram slide`}>Next →</button></div><div class="wx-carousel" tabindex="0" aria-label={`${e.name} Instagram carousel`}>{e.slides.map((s,i)=><figure class={`wx-graphic mat-${i}`}><Image src={s.src} alt={s.alt} widths={[320,540,810,1080]} sizes="(max-width:700px) 76vw, 360px"/><figcaption>0{i+1} / {s.role}</figcaption></figure>)}</div><div class="wx-caption"><span class="wys-label">The complete Instagram caption / publication draft</span><p>{e.caption}</p><p class="wx-fine">The verbal link-in-bio CTA belongs to the eventual authorized posting account. These example slides have not been posted.</p></div></div>
 <div data-panel="4" class="wx-panel"><div class="wx-output-label"><h3>The full article, not a placeholder.</h3><p>This is the actual prepared article used by the live Lifestyle page.</p></div><article class="wx-article-preview"><div class="wx-article-cover"><WysPhoto photo={e.photos[1]} treatment="double" caption={e.category}/><div><span class="wys-label">The Lifestyle edit / article preview</span><h3>{e.article.title}</h3><p>{e.article.intro}</p><a class="wys-button" href={`/lifestyle/${e.slug}`}>Open the complete styling page →</a></div></div>{e.article.sections.map(s=><section><h4>{s.heading}</h4>{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p>{p}</p>)}</section>)}<div class="wx-article-end"><b>The five selected finds</b><ol>{e.article.items.map(item=><li>{item.name} · {item.variant}</li>)}</ol><p class="wx-fine">As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases. Shopping links and Amazon lists are pending. {imageNotice}</p></div></article></div>
 <div data-panel="5" class="wx-panel"><div class="wx-output-label"><h3>The records behind the pretty.</h3><p>Five actual selected product types, plus the copy that carries the look across channels.</p></div><div class="wx-source-layout"><WysPhoto photo={e.photos[0]} treatment="lavender" label="Source look / selected pieces"/><div class="wx-product-records">{e.article.items.map((p,i)=><details open><summary><span>0{i+1}</span>{p.name}</summary><p><b>Selected variant:</b> {p.variant}</p><p>{p.note}</p><p class="wx-fine">Affiliate verification pending. Recorded sourcing is not a live stock guarantee.</p></details>)}</div></div><div class="wx-caption"><span class="wys-label">Instagram caption / ready to review</span><p>{e.caption}</p><p>The Pinterest tab contains all three titles, descriptions, alt texts and article destinations.</p></div><div class="wx-paper-strip"><div><h3>Selected products ≠ styling extras</h3><p>Only the five recorded product types belong to this shopping edit. Room furnishings, flowers, artwork and clothing are inspiration, not silently added products.</p></div><div><h3>Destinations come before posting.</h3><p>Check the actual affiliate links and the correct shopping destination first. A prepared article or graphic does not make an Amazon list submitted or a social post published.</p></div></div></div>
 <footer class="wx-package-status"><b>What you’re viewing:</b> approved AI-generated styling photographs and the actual article records, with newly typeset website-example social graphics and copy. Shopping destinations and social posting remain pending. This is a content walkthrough, not a verified customer automation run.</footer>
</section>
<script>
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-package]').forEach(root=>{
 const buttons=[...root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-panel-button]')];
 const panels=[...root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-panel]')];
 const select=(n:string)=>{buttons.forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b.dataset.panelButton===n)));panels.forEach(p=>p.hidden=p.dataset.panel!==n);};const initial=new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('view');select(location.hash==='#'+root.id&&initial&&/^[0-5]$/.test(initial)?initial:'0');
 buttons.forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>select(b.dataset.panelButton!)));
 const rail=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.wx-carousel')!;const count=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-slide-count]')!;
 const update=()=>{const slides=[...rail.children] as HTMLElement[];const i=slides.reduce((best,s,n)=>Math.abs(s.offsetLeft-rail.offsetLeft-rail.scrollLeft)<Math.abs(slides[best].offsetLeft-rail.offsetLeft-rail.scrollLeft)?n:best,0);count.textContent=`${i+1} / 3`;return i;};
 root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-slide-step]').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>{const n=Math.max(0,Math.min(2,update()+Number(b.dataset.slideStep)));const s=rail.children[n] as HTMLElement;rail.scrollTo({left:s.offsetLeft-rail.offsetLeft,behavior:window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches?'instant':'smooth'});}));rail.addEventListener('scroll',update,{passive:true});
 });
</script>
